Warnings:
Warning	1287	The hypergraph optimizer is highly experimental and is meant for testing only. Do not enable it unless you are a MySQL developer.
# Q13-style NOT LIKE reaches the null-supplying scan after simplification.
EXPLAIN FORMAT=TREE SELECT c.id,o.id FROM outer_push_customer c
LEFT JOIN outer_push_orders o ON c.id=o.customer_id
WHERE NOT (o.comment LIKE '%special%requests%');
EXPLAIN
-> Nested loop inner join  (rows=5.33)
    -> Vectorized table scan on o in secondary engine Rapid [filter: o.comment NOT LIKE %special%requests%]  (rows=3)
    -> Single-row index lookup on c using PRIMARY (id=o.customer_id) in secondary engine Rapid  (rows=1)

Warnings:
Note	1003	Query is executed in secondary engine; the actual query plan may diverge from the printed one
# NULL comments, unmatched customers and customers with only rejected matches.
EXPLAIN FORMAT=TREE SELECT c.id,o.id FROM outer_push_customer c
LEFT JOIN outer_push_orders o ON c.id=o.customer_id WHERE o.comment IS NULL;
EXPLAIN
-> Filter: (o.`comment` is null)
    -> Vectorized left hash join (c.id = o.customer_id)  (rows=6)
        -> Vectorized table scan on c in secondary engine Rapid  (rows=6)
        -> Hash
            -> Vectorized table scan on o in secondary engine Rapid  (rows=6)

Warnings:
Note	1003	Query is executed in secondary engine; the actual query plan may diverge from the printed one
# An anti join must keep the existence test and its inner condition intact.
# A null-rejecting amount predicate prunes a whole IMCU on the orders side.
SELECT COUNT(*) FROM outer_push_customer c LEFT JOIN outer_push_orders o
ON c.id=o.customer_id WHERE o.amount>100000 AND o.comment NOT LIKE '%special%requests%';
COUNT(*)
6
